1
00:00:02,300 --> 00:00:05,409
This video shows you how to review a teammate's change,

2
00:00:05,409 --> 00:00:08,270
ask for what it's missing, and deploy it.

3
00:00:08,320 --> 00:00:09,604
Here's Sam's browser.

4
00:00:09,604 --> 00:00:14,058
Sam wants the pipeline to drop records from the search service.

5
00:00:15,200 --> 00:00:17,490
Sam needs records to try it on.

6
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:21,183
Add a sample and capture from the earliest record.

7
00:00:21,183 --> 00:00:23,334
Three records arrive.

8
00:00:30,680 --> 00:00:35,150
Sam stops the capture and uses these records, without saving them.

9
00:00:35,200 --> 00:00:40,478
Sam adds a Drop step, and drops each record whose service is search.

10
00:00:44,480 --> 00:00:47,430
The preview strikes out the search record.

11
00:00:47,480 --> 00:00:51,189
Sam saves the pipeline, on a branch of its own.

12
00:00:54,720 --> 00:00:56,417
Then opens it for review.

13
00:00:56,417 --> 00:01:01,089
smeltr fills in the title and description from what changed.

14
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:10,251
Sam is an editor, so Approve and deploy stays off.

15
00:01:10,251 --> 00:01:13,710
Deploying this takes a deployer in shared.

16
00:01:13,760 --> 00:01:17,468
In your browser, Branches lists Sam's change.

17
00:01:17,468 --> 00:01:18,727
Open it.

18
00:01:19,960 --> 00:01:25,550
It changes one thing: it adds a Drop step to the pipeline tutorial-in-parse.

19
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:27,710
But no test covers it.

20
00:01:27,760 --> 00:01:28,765
Ask for one.

21
00:01:28,765 --> 00:01:33,048
Say why, choose Request changes, and submit.

22
00:01:36,600 --> 00:01:39,651
Sam sees your request on the change.

23
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,267
A test needs a saved sample.

24
00:01:43,267 --> 00:01:49,466
So in the pipeline, Sam saves the records as the sample tutorial-records.

25
00:02:01,600 --> 00:02:04,194
A test checks only what's on screen.

26
00:02:04,194 --> 00:02:09,261
Sam shows just the service field, which says what got through.

27
00:02:12,960 --> 00:02:19,079
Lock this as a test shows what it will check: checkout, dropped, checkout.

28
00:02:19,079 --> 00:02:21,829
Sam names it and locks it.

29
00:02:22,640 --> 00:02:24,852
Then Sam renames the dataset.

30
00:02:24,852 --> 00:02:28,045
The test doesn't check that field.

31
00:02:35,400 --> 00:02:40,630
Back on your view of the change, the test still passes after Sam's last edit.

32
00:02:40,680 --> 00:02:46,270
Open Tests to read what it checks: the service field, on three rows.

33
00:02:46,320 --> 00:02:47,274
It's ready.

34
00:02:47,274 --> 00:02:49,781
Approve and deploy it.

35
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:58,397
History names Sam as the author, and you as the deployer.

36
00:03:03,960 --> 00:03:05,781
Check on learning.

37
00:03:05,981 --> 00:03:08,509
Sam opened a change to shared.

38
00:03:08,509 --> 00:03:10,626
Who can deploy it?

39
00:03:15,026 --> 00:03:18,929
A deployer in shared, or an administrator.

40
00:03:18,929 --> 00:03:21,573
Sam, an editor, can't.

41
00:03:22,473 --> 00:03:24,949
You wanted a test before deploying.

42
00:03:24,949 --> 00:03:27,176
How did you ask for it?

43
00:03:31,576 --> 00:03:35,945
With Request changes, and a comment that says why.

44
00:03:36,845 --> 00:03:40,919
Next, you connect smeltr to a GitHub repository.
